alwaysApply: false
---
# Python Conventions

- Extend the model through the existing mixin/class pattern (defs, photosynthesis,
  hydraulics, soil); don't duplicate sub-model logic in notebooks or scripts.
- Species parameters live in species_traits.py.
- Config and parameter sets go in YAML files, not hard-coded dicts
  (sensitivity runs: sensitivity_analysis/Phase N - name/config.yaml).
- Docstrings plus type hints on new functions and classes.
- Plots: seaborn whitegrid, serif font stack as in sensitivity_analysis/post_processing.py.
- New notebook versions: copy to _v(N+1); move the superseded version to archive/.
- Outputs go next to their inputs, not in output/:
  - Data processing scripts write processed CSVs and figures into the folder
    holding the raw data (e.g. data/soil_data/vwc_data/).
  - Sensitivity/scenario runs write to their Phase results/<batch_id>/ folder
    (figures in results/<batch_id>/figures/).
- Environment: conda.
